# Employee Management

## Overview

A Java application that demonstrates object-oriented programming by modeling employee records with a custom `Employee` class. The program creates employee objects using multiple constructors, updates employee information through setter methods, and displays employee details using getter methods.

## Features

- Create employee objects with multiple constructors
- Store employee information including name, ID, department, and position
- Modify employee data using accessor and mutator methods
- Display employee information in a formatted output
- Demonstrate object creation and interaction in Java

## Concepts Practiced

- Classes and Objects
- Constructors
- Constructor Overloading
- Encapsulation
- Accessor (Getter) Methods
- Mutator (Setter) Methods
- Object Instantiation

## Files

- `EmployeeManagement.java`

## Skills Demonstrated

- Designing reusable Java classes
- Implementing object-oriented programming principles
- Using encapsulation to protect class data
- Creating and managing multiple objects
- Applying constructor overloading to provide flexible object initialization
